### ==============================================================================
### PROJECT 1: BASIC GREETING & HEALTH API (PORT 8000)
### ==============================================================================

### 1. Root Welcome Message
GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/
Accept: application/json

### 2. Service Health Check
GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/health
Accept: application/json

### 3. Nonexistent Route (Should return 404)
GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/nonexistent-route
Accept: application/json


### ==============================================================================
### PROJECT 2: TASK MANAGEMENT IN-MEMORY CRUD API (PORT 8001)
### ==============================================================================

### 1. Root Message
GET http://127.0.0.1:8001/
Accept: application/json

### 2. List All Tasks (Initially Empty)
GET http://127.0.0.1:8001/tasks
Accept: application/json

### 3. Create Task 1 (Valid)
POST http://127.0.0.1:8001/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Learn FastAPI & Pydantic",
  "completed": false
}

### 4. Create Task 2 (Valid - Defaults completed to false)
POST http://127.0.0.1:8001/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Prepare Instructor Presentation"
}

### 5. Create Task (Invalid - Empty Title, should return 422)
POST http://127.0.0.1:8001/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "",
  "completed": false
}

### 6. Create Task (Invalid - Only Whitespace, should return 422)
POST http://127.0.0.1:8001/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "    ",
  "completed": false
}

### 7. Get Task by ID (ID: 1)
GET http://127.0.0.1:8001/tasks/1
Accept: application/json

### 8. Get Nonexistent Task (Should return 404)
GET http://127.0.0.1:8001/tasks/999
Accept: application/json

### 9. Update Task (ID: 1 - Mark Completed)
PUT http://127.0.0.1:8001/tasks/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Learn FastAPI & Pydantic (Completed)",
  "completed": true
}

### 10. Delete Task (ID: 1 - Should return 204 No Content)
DELETE http://127.0.0.1:8001/tasks/1

### 11. Verify Deletion (Should return 404)
GET http://127.0.0.1:8001/tasks/1
Accept: application/json


### ==============================================================================
### PROJECT 3: PERSISTENT SQLITE + SQLALCHEMY API (PORT 8002)
### ==============================================================================

### 1. Root Welcome & Persistence Info
GET http://127.0.0.1:8002/
Accept: application/json

### 2. List Tasks from SQLite
GET http://127.0.0.1:8002/tasks
Accept: application/json

### 3. Create Persistent Task
POST http://127.0.0.1:8002/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Task Saved to SQLite Disk Database",
  "completed": false
}

### 4. Retrieve Saved Task by ID (ID: 1)
GET http://127.0.0.1:8002/tasks/1
Accept: application/json

### 5. Update Persistent Task
PUT http://127.0.0.1:8002/tasks/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Task Saved to SQLite Disk Database (Updated)",
  "completed": true
}

### 6. Delete Persistent Task
DELETE http://127.0.0.1:8002/tasks/1


### ==============================================================================
### PROJECT 4: JWT AUTHENTICATION & SECURITY (PORT 8003)
### ==============================================================================

### 1. Public Welcome
GET http://127.0.0.1:8003/
Accept: application/json

### 2. Register New User
POST http://127.0.0.1:8003/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "developer",
  "password": "supersecretpassword123"
}

### 3. Login to get JWT Token
# @name login
POST http://127.0.0.1:8003/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "developer",
  "password": "supersecretpassword123"
}

### 4. Access Protected Profile (Replace YOUR_TOKEN_HERE with token from login response)
GET http://127.0.0.1:8003/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN_HERE
Accept: application/json

### 5. Access Protected Confidential Vault Data
GET http://127.0.0.1:8003/protected-data
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN_HERE
Accept: application/json

### 6. Attempt Unauthorized Access (Should return 401/403)
GET http://127.0.0.1:8003/protected-data
Accept: application/json
